# Copy to backend/.env and fill in real values; the copy is gitignored.
# Every setting maps to a RAG_-prefixed field in backend/app/core/config.py;
# unset variables fall back to the defaults there. The file is read directly
# by the backend (when started from backend/) and injected into the compose
# api service (deploy/docker-compose.yml) as a required env file, where the
# compose environment block still wins. The test and e2e suites pin the stub
# provider, so this file never makes them call Groq.

# Signs the access tokens (HS256). The value below matches the pydantic
# fallback so local runs behave exactly as before; generate a real one
# (`openssl rand -hex 32`) for any deployment others can reach. The compose
# api service requires this file, so a stack cannot boot without an explicit
# key in place.
RAG_JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me

# Opting in to real answers; the default stub provider keeps the stack offline.
#RAG_LLM_PROVIDER=groq
#RAG_GROQ_API_KEY=

# Production mode is a deployment concern, not a local one: its validators in
# backend/app/core/config.py demand explicit secrets, and the local compose
# stack interpolates its development values from deploy/.env, so do not set
# RAG_ENVIRONMENT here.